  "$comment": "DEVELOPMENT descriptor for the gliner2_decide family (hfmodels-litert, not in the bundled catalog). Generated by tools/hfmodels_descriptor.py from the Hub at the pinned revision: every file's bytes and sha256 are the Hub's, except the two local files named below. The device gate side-loads the files from /data/local/tmp/hfmodels/gliner-decide (GlinerDecideDeviceTest). The draft for the repo's own hfmodels.json. After the three default graphs: s128_npu_wfp16 is the s128 graph re-authored for the Qualcomm HTP in the H2H-2 run h2b2 (2026-09-30: LayerNorm power-of-two pre-scale on 22 norms, a -1e4 attention-mask constant, FC1 split into two FULLY_CONNECTED joined by CONCATENATION; exact in fp32), published at this revision as gliner25_decide_s128_npu_wfp16.tflite, with an npu profile asked for by name (BackendPolicy.Require, no fallback; gpu stays the default, in FP16 with FP32 accumulation as in the bundled catalog); s256_npu_wfp16 and s512_fp16hw_wfp16 are the same re-authoring at 256 and 512 tokens (2026-10-04: 26 and 25 pre-scaled norms), local files that are not on the Hub yet, under the names they would have there (s256 with an npu profile like s128's; s512 without one: the GPU in FP16 with FP32 accumulation, then the CPU); s128_fp32 is the Hub's fp32/ reference graph (a development variant, the CPU fp32 row).",
  "tasks": [
    "decide"
  ],
